    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-floor production today, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jacob Wilson** (70.97). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a premier combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a favorable matchup against Hughes, providing a massive 14% park-factor boost. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** is the day's primary beneficiary of a soft pitching matchup; he faces Me. Kelly (5.31 xERA), and our analytics project his top-of-the-order role and aggressive approach to exploit that skill gap, netting a 19% boost from the SP matchup alone. **Drake Baldwin** (67.31) also demands attention; despite a lingering rain risk, his leadoff spot and strong xwOBA suggest he is the premier source of value behind the dish.\n\nWe were forced to make a difficult cut with **Brayan Rocchio** (56.97), who narrowly missed the starting lineup. While his SP-matchup index against Ober was strong (+16%), his lower base projection relative to the high-upside plays like **Kyle Tucker** (66.04) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.89) kept him on the bench. We are prioritizing the higher ceiling of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** despite the tougher matchup against Jax, banking on his elite underlying power profile to overcome a sub-optimal platoon split.\n\nCaution is advised regarding the weather in our middle-to-lower order. **Dominic Smith** (56.48), **Jackson Merrill** (57.35), and **Drake Baldwin** all face a 35% rain risk, which adds a layer of volatility to their afternoon. Furthermore, while **Gunnar Henderson** (61.28) remains a core asset, he faces a significant 15% dynamic platoon penalty today against the lefty Bennett. We are comfortable holding him in the lineup due to his high base projection and favorable park factors, but his performance will be the primary barometer for the team\u2019s success in a high-variance environment.",
